<h2 id="who-its-for" style="margin-top:2rem;">🎯 Who Each Platform Is For</h2>

<p><strong>Choose Moosend if:</strong> You're a D2C brand under $5M in annual revenue, your email team is lean or non-technical, you want a capable platform without Klaviyo-level spend, or you're launching a new brand and want to keep fixed costs tight while you find product-market fit. It's also a strong pick for WooCommerce and Magento operators who don't benefit from Klaviyo's Shopify-specific advantages. Operators managing multiple brands under a holding company will appreciate Moosend's cost structure across accounts.</p>

<p><strong>Choose Klaviyo if:</strong> You're on Shopify, your revenue is above $5M, you actively use predictive segmentation in flows, you want SMS and email in one platform with shared audience logic, or your retention team runs sophisticated multi-channel journeys that require Klaviyo's conditional logic depth. At this scale, Klaviyo's incremental revenue lift from better segmentation generally justifies the cost premium.</p>

<p>We've seen brands make the wrong call in both directions. A $500K DTC skincare brand paying $700/month for Klaviyo features they never touch is burning margin. Equally, a $10M apparel brand trying to run complex loyalty-tier automation on a platform without predictive scoring is leaving revenue on the table. Match the tool to your actual operational maturity, not your aspirational one. Check our <a href="https://ecommerceoperator.io/guides/email-automation-for-ecommerce">email automation guide for ecommerce</a> to calibrate where your program actually sits.</p>

